From d56802182e0daf0a2b07175ab7f7de954224f91e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tillmann Severin <tillmann.severin@mailbox.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:16:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/24] arm64: defconfig: enable Hi3798MV200 peripherals

Enable the drivers needed by the Hi3798MV200 that were not already
selected: the SoC specific dw_mmc extension for the SD and eMMC hosts,
the hix5hd2 I2C controller and the hix5hd2 IR receiver.

The gigabit MAC (CONFIG_HIX5HD2_GMAC) and the Realtek PHY driver are
already enabled, and COMMON_CLK_HI3798MV200 is selected automatically by
its "default ARCH_HISI".

The IR driver is built as a module so that RC_CORE can stay a module for
all the other arm64 platforms.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index 32861d08a3b8..d4d52e56f7b8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -533,6 +533,7 @@ CONFIG_I2C_CHARDEV=y
 CONFIG_I2C_MUX=y
 CONFIG_I2C_MUX_PCA954x=y
 CONFIG_I2C_MUX_PINCTRL=m
+CONFIG_I2C_HIX5HD2=y
 CONFIG_I2C_BCM2835=m
 CONFIG_I2C_CADENCE=m
 CONFIG_I2C_DESIGNWARE_CORE=y
@@ -842,6 +843,7 @@ CONFIG_RC_CORE=m
 CONFIG_RC_DECODERS=y
 CONFIG_RC_DEVICES=y
 CONFIG_IR_GPIO_CIR=m
+CONFIG_IR_HIX5HD2=m
 CONFIG_IR_MESON=m
 CONFIG_IR_SUNXI=m
 CONFIG_MEDIA_CEC_SUPPORT=y
@@ -1211,6 +1213,7 @@ CONFIG_MMC_UNIPHIER=y
 CONFIG_MMC_DW=y
 CONFIG_MMC_DW_EXYNOS=y
 CONFIG_MMC_DW_HI3798CV200=y
+CONFIG_MMC_DW_HI3798MV200=y
 CONFIG_MMC_DW_K3=y
 CONFIG_MMC_DW_ROCKCHIP=y
 CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI=y
-- 
